Current Dev Position: YP 2.3 M2

Next Deadline: YP 2.3 M2 by Jan 23, 2017


SWAT team rotation: Saul -> Paul on Jan. 20, 2017.

SWAT team rotation: Paul -> Ross on Jan. 27, 2017.

https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Yocto_Build_Failure_Swat_Team


Key Status/Updates:

=B7        The 2.2.1 release has been held up by a bug in eSDK which we now=
 know was =91fixed=92 by some of the tinfoil2 changes. Those clearly won=92=
t be backported to 2.2 so we=92re looking into what we need to do to fix th=
is in 2.2 instead.

=B7        Master has continued to be problematic to merge patches into. We=
 have tracked down a glibc 2.25 issue with python3 on older hosts (e.g. cen=
tos7) which was causing some hard to isolate autobuilder failures.

=B7        The M2 deadline has now passed. We were able to merge the oeqa r=
ewrite and recipe specific sysroot patches. Unfortunately as yet we still d=
on=92t know the exact performance impact of this change but we=92ve opted t=
o move forward with it regardless.

=B7        Master now contains all the patches we=92ve been able to get to =
work cleanly. Examples of things which did not merge are the linux-libc-hea=
ders (due to musl issues) but we did merge the actual kernel updates and th=
e container changes as the selftests didn=92t pass.

=B7        Since master builds cleanly and has a lot of change in as it sta=
nds, we=92re tempted just to call this good for M2 and start the QA cycle.

=B7        One particular challenge we continue to face is the length of ti=
me oe-selftest takes to run and we plan to have a focus on this during M3.


Proposed upcoming dot releases:

YP 2.2.1 Release by Jan. 20, 2017 (Will be after YP 2.3 M2 is out of QA)

YP 2.1.3 Cut off May 8, 2017

YP 2.1.3 Release by May 19, 2017

